#   A = baseline (flow-stats + keep port/protocol/flags)  [NO IP-aggregate behavior]
#   B = behavior-enriched (includes protocol/port semantics + throughput/duration logs + IP-based aggregates)
#
# Split: GROUP SPLIT by IPV4_SRC_ADDR (no src_ip overlap between train/test)
# Notes:
# - We do NOT feed raw IP strings to the model. We only use IP to compute behavior stats.
# - Behavior stats computed WITHIN EACH SPLIT (train/test separately), past-only (time sorted).
# - Additionally: remove exact-duplicate feature rows across splits (DEDUP_COLS hash) to prevent RF ~100%.
# - Extra drop: strong proxy-like features (apply to BOTH A and B for fair ablation) with 2 modes:
#     * PROXY_DROP_MODE="light" (recommended first)
#     * PROXY_DROP_MODE="hard"  (stress)

